Cell["\<\
All states at one step are paths of the same length. They are separate states \
because they were reached by different histories, that is, by splitting the \
edges in a different order.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->2122865143,ExpressionUUID->"07964fa7-8d1e-ff14-2dae-660124a8c27e"],

Cell["The evolution graph", "Section",
 CellID->1735808809,ExpressionUUID->"3e367b18-9aa8-58f9-67ce-73421f5d2ac3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<EvolutionGraph\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1dbaaaf7-1388-e538-4b59-43b1a622cc02"],
 " also draws the events. A state is a blue box. An event is a yellow box \
showing its input state, with the consumed edge dashed, and its output state, \
with the produced edges highlighted. Gray edges lead from a state to its \
events and from an event to its output state."
}], "Text",
 CellID->753514147,ExpressionUUID->"77d99fdb-a351-2d53-1de6-1684d6e477b9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Two steps of the chain rule; the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["AspectRatio"]], "paclet:ref/AspectRatio"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "04646437-faee-7dfc-2c1c-7e70fe9b47c6"],
 " option sets the height of the graph relative to its width:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1164297175,ExpressionUUID->"1cbde497-e826-5557-4442-fdd089d33fbd"],

